# q36-35b-a3b-fp8.recipe -- Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8 with its MTP head, as the q36-35b-a3b-fp8.rad
# container serves it.
#
#   rad-convert <Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8 checkpoint> --recipe data/recipes/q36-35b-a3b-fp8.recipe \
#       -o q36-35b-a3b-fp8.rad
#
# The linears -- attention, delta net, shared and routed experts, the MTP layer's -- are
# block-scaled fp8 in the checkpoint and kept as they are. What the recipe adds:
#
#   - the lm_head, block fp8: the widest GEMM in the model at half the bytes
#   - the MTP head's 2-bit copy of the lm_head (u2 codes, an f16 scale and a u8 zero a group of
#     128), which the draft rounds read in place of the full head

output.weight                        rtn  codes=fp8_e4m3 block=128x128 scale=bf16
mtp.draft_head.weight                rtn  codes=u2 zero=u8 group=128 scale=f16
